Z||000000||Cozmo||06-05-2001||07:31 AM||||Just ordered a MSD blaster coil from Summit for the 2M6 targa.  I remember reading somewhere (can't find it now, of course) that you should increase the spark plug gap th take advantage of the MSDs' higher output voltage.  I think the suggestion was .060".<BR>I currently have (all NEW parts):<BR>GM ignition module and pickup coil<BR>ACDelco rapidfires gapped at (factory) .045"<BR>Wells cap and rotor<BR>AutoZone 8mm wires<BR>The car runs great, but seems to lose a little "poop" above 4000 RPM.  <BR>Would the gap change (.045" to .060") make any difference (good or bad) or am I smokin' bad s**t again? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">?<BR><B>C02M0</B><P>------------------<BR><B>C02M0</B><BR><I>Suncoast Fieros</I><BR>'85 silver 2M6 4spd. Targa <B>"Silver Streak"</B><BR>'86 black auto GT <B>"Blackbird"</B><BR>'87 white auto Coupe <B>"The Duke"</B>||||reg||5
